Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ===========================================================================
;  02_clsid_inprocserver.reg
;  Point the 32-bit COM in-process server for the VirtualBox object at our
;  shim, so eNSP (a 32-bit process) loads VBox52.dll when it creates it.
;
;  CLSID {B1A7A4F2-47B9-4A1E-82B2-07CCD5323C3F} = CLSID_VirtualBox (the main
;  IVirtualBox object). VBox52.dll exports DllGetClassObject and hands eNSP a
;  5.2-shaped interface bridged onto the real 7.2 VBoxSVC.
;
;  32-bit view (WOW6432Node) ONLY. A stock VirtualBox 7.2.16 has no such key in
;  the 32-bit view at all, and in the 64-bit view only LocalServer32
;  (-> VBoxSVC.exe). Do not add an InprocServer32 to the 64-bit view: it points
;  64-bit clients at a 32-bit DLL and they fail with 0x800700C1 (measured).
;  This is what installer\install.ps1 writes as well.
;
;  Edit the path below if eNSP is not installed under C:\Program Files\Huawei.
;  To undo: reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Classes\WOW6432Node\CLSID\{B1A7A4F2-47B9-4A1E-82B2-07CCD5323C3F}" /f
; ===========================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Classes\WOW6432Node\CLSID\{B1A7A4F2-47B9-4A1E-82B2-07CCD5323C3F}\InprocServer32]
@="C:\\Program Files\\Huawei\\eNSP\\tools\\VBox52.dll"
"ThreadingModel"="Both"
